{"name":"White Shoulders","hex":"#f1f0ec","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"},{"term":"shoulders","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of shoulder","The two shoulders and the upper portion of the back."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of shoulder"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoulders"}],"entries":[{"title":"White Shoulders","blocks":[{"text":"White Shoulders is a lost 1931 American pre-Code comedy-drama film directed by Melville W. Brown and starring Mary Astor and Jack Holt, with major supporting roles by Ricardo Cortez and Sidney Toler. The film was produced and distributed by RKO Pictures. The screenplay by Jane Murfin and J. Walter Ruben was adapted from Rex Beach's short story, The Recoil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/White_Shoulders_poster.jpg/330px-White_Shoulders_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Shoulders","wikidata":"Q7995389"},{"title":"White Shoulders (fragrance)","blocks":[{"text":"White Shoulders is a white floral fragrance released in 1943 by spouses Walter (\"Peter\") Langer and Diane Evelyn (\"Evyan\") Langer, who incorporated Evyan Perfumes, Inc., in 1946."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Shoulders_(fragrance)","wikidata":"Q141308811"},{"title":"Shoulder","blocks":[{"text":"The human shoulder is made up of three bones: the clavicle (collarbone), the scapula, and the humerus as well as associated muscles, ligaments and tendons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Left_shoulder.jpg/330px-Left_shoulder.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoulder","wikidata":"Q16363"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/WhiteShoulders.HoltAstorCortez.jpg/250px-WhiteShoulders.HoltAstorCortez.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f8/WhiteShoulders.HoltAstorCortez.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/WhiteShoulders.HoltAstorCortez.jpg/250px-WhiteShoulders.HoltAstorCortez.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Holt, Astor and Cortez","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhiteShoulders.HoltAstorCortez.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Gray327.png/500px-Gray327.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Gray327.png/500px-Gray327.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGray327.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Blausen_0797_ShoulderJoint.png/500px-Blausen_0797_ShoulderJoint.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Blausen_0797_ShoulderJoint.png/1280px-Blausen_0797_ShoulderJoint.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Blausen_0797_ShoulderJoint.png/500px-Blausen_0797_ShoulderJoint.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cross-section of shoulder joint","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlausen_0797_ShoulderJoint.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Gray523.png/500px-Gray523.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Gray523.png/500px-Gray523.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The brachial plexus surrounds the axillary artery and is formed from nerve roots from C5-T1. Branches of the plexus supply the shoulder region, although several other nerves play a role.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGray523.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Grant_1962_664.png/500px-Grant_1962_664.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Grant_1962_664.png/1280px-Grant_1962_664.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Grant_1962_664.png/500px-Grant_1962_664.png?utm_source=en.wi